                You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Noah</span> how things have been at home since you talked during your stormy night encounter. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I don’t know.”</span> He shrugs, fiddling with his shoelace, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I know I don’t have to be shy anymore, since I love you and Daddy and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span>, but it still feels weird. I thought about talking with Daddy about all that stuff, but he already gets mad at grandma when she calls, so I didn’t want to cause trouble.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Noah</span> looks up at you with a smile, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But I did tell Daddy he can give me baths again, if he wants. He seemed happy about that.”</span> You hug <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Noah</span> happily, asking if you could give him a bath sometime. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You only want to do it so you can touch my thingy!”</span> He teases, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But I guess so.”</span> <br>
